    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medication: continued without change, Donepezil 10 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth daily in the morning [S]</item><item>Medication: continued without change, Cholecalciferol 50 mcg (2,000 units) oral tablet, one tablet by mouth daily [S]</item><item>Goal: Walk household distances with a walker and supervision, with a Barthel Index of 75 or more, by the three-month visit. Outcome by 2001-04-14: Barthel Index rose from 55 to 75; walks in the house and garden with a walker [S]</item><item>Goal: 25-hydroxyvitamin D of 30 ng/mL or more by three months, then the first zoledronic acid infusion. Outcome by 2001-04-14: 25-hydroxyvitamin D 36 ng/mL; zoledronic acid given [S]</item><item>Goal: No further falls through the six-month visit. Outcome by 2001-07-14: No falls; Timed Up and Go improved from 24 to 16 seconds [S]</item><item>Goal: Lower the spouse&apos;s Zarit Burden Interview score by at least 10 points by six months. Outcome by 2001-07-14: Zarit score fell from 41 to 27 with weekly respite, a home health aide, and caregiver education [S]</item><item>Goal: Document a health care agent, goals of care, and a POLST form by the three-month visit. Outcome by 2001-04-14: Health care agent confirmed and POLST completed with the patient and spouse [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 2001-02-10 [S]</item><item>Scheduled episode complete. Continue routine follow-up [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
